---
module: plain_parser
func_id: write-parse-output
---

***conformance tests***

# utf8-whatever-the-encoding
A module whose functionality body ends with ` It greets “Zoë” with ✓.`, parsed in a process whose standard output encoding is ASCII, exits with code 0, writes nothing on standard error, and its standard output decoded as UTF-8 is JSON holding `“Zoë” with ✓`.

# closed-pipe
`parse valid.plain` in a process whose standard output is a pipe already closed by the reader exits with code 0 and writes nothing on standard error.

# non-utf8-directory-stays-out
A module in a directory whose name holds the byte 0xff, linking `notes.md` next to it, parsed from the parent directory, exits with code 0 and prints the resources {`notes.md`: `notes.md`}.

***acceptance tests***

# non-utf8-module-name
A module file whose name is `bad` + byte 0xff + `name.plain`, parsed from its directory, exits with code 1, writes nothing on standard error, and prints the message `The parse result holds text that is not valid UTF-8: "module": "bad\udcffname"`.

# non-utf8-path-in-error
A module in a directory whose name holds the byte 0xff, linking the missing `missing.md`, prints the type `PlainSyntaxError` and a message holding `bad\udcffname`.

# result-not-json
When the parse result holds a value JSON cannot represent, `parse` exits with code 1, writes nothing on standard error, and prints the type `TypeError`.
